                    {
                        "translation_id": "3972945a-10e8-4ffd-ba1a-69c96aa72fa1",
                        "source_entry_id": "8402070b-445e-396c-a11f-f2473f930bed",
                        "source_sense_id": "528bf6f8-8f8d-3e89-a337-880810125afb",
                        "target_lang_word": "ragga",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ragga",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28ba2ff2-e137-3350-a6cb-795f1ceae1fb",
                                        "entry_id": "82e2e6e2-3dc6-37b1-8ae3-36bd189da30f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A subgenre of reggae and dancehall influenced by hip hop and digital production techniques such as sampling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78d4b9f6-b252-4dd4-affd-d8c3dd352609",
                                                "sense_id": "28ba2ff2-e137-3350-a6cb-795f1ceae1fb",
                                                "text": "Tosh's brand of roots reggae, with its emphasis on uplifting anthems and melodic riffs, now sounds as dated as The Wailers' earliest incarnation as a straight-up ska band, especially when listened to alongside the shuddering bass of most contemporary ragga tracks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb709c45-2bbe-4009-b176-5563229805df",
                                                "sense_id": "28ba2ff2-e137-3350-a6cb-795f1ceae1fb",
                                                "text": "The song samples Ricky Martin's hit Shake Your Bom-Bom but adds ragga's roughness. When Bam Bam comes on, the crowd goes wild."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0bc5600-f862-4a21-828a-5a2fd78fce51",
                                                "sense_id": "28ba2ff2-e137-3350-a6cb-795f1ceae1fb",
                                                "text": "A sub-genre of reggae, ragga is a modern Jamaican sound with ties to the oldest traditional music of that island-nation. The name is taken from the word “raggamuffin”, a term used for disenfranchised youth. One popular ragga singer called Half Pint said, “A lot of people interpret raggamuffin as if it [is]^([sic]) a criminal morality.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7395cc6b-30c7-4a9d-b01c-1069ce886574",
                                                "sense_id": "28ba2ff2-e137-3350-a6cb-795f1ceae1fb",
                                                "text": "Fling a ragga riddim like it's '03"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
